# ── secrets: never commit ──────────────────────────────
#
# Case matters, and it nearly cost us. `*credentials*` alone does NOT match
# CREDENTIALS.md on a case-sensitive filesystem — it matched on this Windows box
# only because core.ignorecase=true. Every Linux checkout, CI runner and GitHub
# Action loses the protection, and the 2026-08-17 near-miss (StartUp.md §13) was
# stopped by a control that only works on one developer's machine. Globs here are
# spelled case-insensitively rather than trusting the filesystem.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.p8
*.jks
*.keystore
auth.json
oauth2*.json
.netrc
.npmrc
id_rsa*
*[Cc][Rr][Ee][Dd][Ee][Nn][Tt][Ii][Aa][Ll]*
*[Ss][Ee][Cc][Rr][Ee][Tt]*
*.stackdump

# ── dependencies / build ──────────────────────────────
/vendor
/composer.phar
/node_modules
/public/build
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/framework/cache/*
/storage/framework/sessions/*
/storage/framework/views/*
/storage/logs/*
!/storage/**/.gitkeep

# ── local ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
.cursor/agent-mail-stall.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# Flutter web build output — derived, not source. Built locally and uploaded to
# the shared directory on the server (see scripts/deploy.sh). 36 MB per build,
# almost all CanvasKit, and a new blob on every rebuild: committing it would
# bloat the repo permanently for no gain.
/public/app

# Release artefacts — installers and app bundles, produced by scripts/release.sh.
# Derived from a commit, tens of MB each, and a fresh blob on every build. They
# are uploaded to Play and handed to testers, not versioned here.
/dist

# PHPUnit's test-result cache. Rewritten by every run, so tracking it made the
# tree dirty after any test and blocked release.sh. Laravel gitignores it by
# default; this repo had it committed.
.phpunit.result.cache

# Scratch output from the Playwright MCP browser. Session artefacts, never source.
/.playwright-mcp/

# App Store screenshots, produced by scripts/screenshots-ios.sh from the real
# app on a simulator. Derived output: 2.7 MB of PNGs that this repo would push
# to the production server on every deploy, and that any machine with the
# simulator can regenerate.
/store-screenshots/

# Laravel's schema dump. NOT committed, deliberately.
#
# It makes the server's deploy gate much faster — one file load instead of
# replaying 82 migrations, each paying two fsyncs on a busy disk. But Laravel
# LOADS it by shelling out to the `mysql` client, and on the Windows dev
# machines the MySQL bin directory is not on PATH, so every local test run dies
# with "'mysql' is not recognized" the moment this file exists.
#
# Breaking every developer's local loop to speed up one server step is the wrong
# trade. The deploy dying was never this anyway — that was an SSH idle timeout,
# fixed with ServerAliveInterval. Revisit if the bin dir gets onto PATH and
# DEV-ENVIRONMENT.md says so.
/database/schema/
